From: Xperia Hikari mainline project <xperia-hikari@localhost>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 13:10:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: skip unreliable MSM8x60 DSI pixel halt status

The MSM8x60 multimedia debug-bus vector does not reliably report the DSI
pixel gate state on Hikari.  Physical boot testing shows bit 6 of register
0x01d0 remains asserted after enabling the gate at 0x0130, causing the common
clock framework to return -EBUSY and roll the whole DSI link-clock sequence
back.  Sony's vendor DSI path programs 0x0130 directly and does not poll this
debug-bus bit.

Keep the real gate operation, but skip only the invalid halt readback.  This
matches the existing treatment of the adjacent MSM8x60 DSI core clock.

Signed-off-by: Xperia Hikari mainline project <xperia-hikari@localhost>
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8660.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8660.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8660.c
index 18404a81483a..a7da7300477c 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8660.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8660.c
@@ -709,6 +709,14 @@ static struct clk_rcg dsi1_pixel_src = {
 static struct clk_branch dsi1_pixel_clk = {
 	.halt_reg = 0x01d0,
 	.halt_bit = 6,
+	/*
+	 * Hikari physical boot evidence shows this debug-bus bit remains set
+	 * while the 0x0130 gate is enabled.  Polling it therefore rejects a
+	 * working vendor-defined clock sequence with -EBUSY.  Sony's MSM8x60
+	 * DSI code writes the gate directly without a halt-status readback,
+	 * as is already required for dsi1_clk above.
+	 */
+	.halt_check = BRANCH_HALT_SKIP,
 	.clkr = {
 		.enable_reg = 0x0130,
 		.enable_mask = BIT(0),
-- 
2.51.0
